# Document 9 — Technical Roadmap

This technical roadmap defines the precise sequence of engineering tasks to build **Koinonia** as an installable Progressive Web App (PWA) using **Next.js**, **Supabase** (Auth, Postgres RLS, Realtime), **LiveKit** (WebRTC audio/video/screen share), and **Cloudinary** (media optimization).

---

### Phase 1: Foundational Architecture & Core Database (Weeks 1 – 2)

#### 1. Setup & Environment Configuration

* Initialize Next.js project with Tailwind CSS, TypeScript, and `@ducanh2912/next-pwa` (or equivalent PWA plugin) to configure `manifest.json`, web icons, and offline service worker fallback.
* Configure Supabase project with environment variables (`NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`).
* Configure Cloudinary API credentials and upload presets for profile avatars and group media.

#### 2. Database Schema & Row-Level Security (RLS) Implementation

Execute initial PostgreSQL migrations in Supabase:

* `profiles`: `id (FK to auth.users)`, `full_name`, `avatar_url`, `time_zone`, `created_at`.
* `fellowships`: `id`, `name`, `description`, `cover_image_url`, `created_by (FK profiles)`, `invite_code (UNIQUE)`, `is_private (BOOLEAN)`.
* `fellowship_members`: `id`, `fellowship_id (FK)`, `user_id (FK)`, `role ('host' | 'member')`, `joined_at`.
* `channels`: `id`, `fellowship_id (FK)`, `name`, `type ('chat' | 'prayer_board' | 'notes')`.
* `messages`: `id`, `channel_id (FK)`, `user_id (FK)`, `content`, `attachment_url`, `created_at`.
* `prayer_requests`: `id`, `fellowship_id (FK)`, `user_id (FK)`, `title`, `description`, `status ('active' | 'answered')`, `created_at`.
